# Data files are bytes, not text — git must never rewrite their line endings.
#
# Without this, committing from Windows normalises CRLF to LF in the repo while the
# Linux refresh runner regenerates CRLF, so every scheduled run saw all 7 CSVs as
# "changed" and committed them. That fired once (b7dd39b) before it was caught. The
# generator now pins lineterminator="\n"; this makes the guarantee independent of who
# runs it and from which platform.
data/**  -text
*.csv    -text
*.json   -text
